research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1006-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1007-## Statement
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1008-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1009-**False claim:** let $A \subseteq \mathbb{R}$, let $c$ be a limit point of $A$
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1010-([[def-limit-point-r]]) and let $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$ have a limit at $c$
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1011-([[def-function-limit]]). Then $f$ is bounded on $A$, that is, the image $f(A)$
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1012-is a bounded subset of $\mathbb{R}$ ([[def-bounded-set]]).
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1013-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1014-**What is true is the local statement**,
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md:1015:[[lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness]]: there is a *radius* $\delta > 0$ such
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1016-that $f$ is bounded on $A \cap N^{*}_{\delta}(c)$. The radius is produced by the
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1017-limit condition at the single tolerance $\varepsilon = 1$, and it carries no
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1018-information whatever about the values of $f$ far from $c$, which the limit
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1019-condition never constrains.
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1020-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1021-The witness below is $f(x) = 1/x$ on $(0, \infty)$ at the point $c = 1$: the
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1022-limit there is $1$, and $f$ is bounded near $1$, while on the whole domain
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1023-$f$ takes values above every real.
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1024-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1025-## Facts & Assumptions
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1026-
research/audit/wave7-refuter-tasks/lem-limit-implies-local-boundedness.md-1027-**Given:** The set $A := (0, \infty)$ ([[def-interval]]), the point $c := 1$, and the function $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$ with $f(x) := 1/x = x^{-1}$.
