research/audit/wave5-dispatch/audit-alpha-wave5-a8-round3.result.json:16:  "tail": "A8 round 3 is complete. **No items edited** — zero `confirmed_fatal`, so nothing to rejudge and A8 closes immediately.\n\n## Rulings\n\n| # | item | model | ruling |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit` | deepseek | **false_positive** (4th) |\n| 2 | `cex-strictly-decreasing-gaps-no-limit` | deepseek | confirmed_nonfatal |\n| 3 | `cor-monotone-converges-iff-bounded` | deepseek | confirmed_nonfatal |\n| 4 | `ex-nested-intervals-single-point` | deepseek | confirmed_nonfatal |\n| 5 | `ex-two-subsequential-limits` | deepseek | confirmed_nonfatal |\n| 6 | `lem-cauchy-sequence-bounded` | sonnet | confirmed_nonfatal |\n\nEvidence, one line each:\n1. `fs-rationals-complete` has a full Refutation establishing every `[L1]` clause verbatim — *\"set $s_n = k_n/10^n$; then $s_n^2 \\le 2 < (s_n+10^{-n})^2$\"*, *\"$(s_n)$ is Cauchy\"*, *\"no rational limit\"*. The judge read the refuted claim as the page's whole content.\n2. `lem-power-monotone` supplies `[L3]`'s other clause exactly; the binomial identity is distributivity, and step 2.2 co-cites `[L1]` ordered-field arithmetic.\n3. `lem-of-abs-value` states *\"$-|x| \\le x \\le |x|$\"* verbatim, and step 1.2 uses only the forward direction off that chain.\n4. The clause is `def-abs-value`'s first branch and appears verbatim as `[L1]` *inside* the cited `lem-of-abs-value`.\n5. Three of four `[L5]` clauses are verbatim; the fourth is one case split on $|t| \\in \\{t,-t\\}$, and step 4.1 already co-cites `[L9]` trichotomy.\n6. The Remark does **not** assert a converse the library lacks — `thm-cauchy-criterion-via-lub` *is* the library's Cauchy⇒convergent and is named in the same parenthetical doing all the work. `lem-convergent-implies-cauchy` is mis-slotted, doing none.\n\n**Twice-touched:** `cor-monotone-converges-iff-bounded` — escalated to your personal audit per the standing rule; ruled nonfatal, no fix. Against my round-2 stopping condition (a third distinct *fatal* reopens the Statement), a third nonfatal does not.\n\n## Two things to correct on your side\n\n**The dispatch's item hashes were the wrong normalisation.** All six came from `judge.mts`'s hash (only the `judge:` sub-block stripped); the adjudication ledger is consumed by `step8-guard`, which compares against `item-hash.mjs` (whole `verification:` block stripped). Copying them in would have written rows the guard can never match. The derived claim was also false: `cex-cauchy-rationals-no-rational-limit` has **not** changed — its normalised hash is still `beede7a2a1…`, identical to all three prior `false_positive` rows. Same for four of the other five. The apparent movement was a judge stamp.\n\n**A concurrent process edited `library/topology/function-space-topologies.md` at 03:08:30, inside my window.** Not mine — I made no write under `library/` or `items/`. It looks like a correct published-claim-decay prose fix, and I left it in place. But note `step8-guard` tracks `items/` only, so a `library/` page edit passes R1 silently even though R1's text forbids page mutation at A8. It did not stale the receipt: my gate run at 03:09:44 came after it and still returned 209/209, because clause (b) of commit `3bbae7f` covered every item on the page — first live confirmation that fix works, worth ~31 rejudge calls.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `step8-guard` (`pre-a8-round3`): **OK** — 2767 items, 0 changed\n- `level-coverage --audit`: **exit 0** — 209 items, 209 complete judge pairs\n- `level-coverage --verify-current-context`: **exit 0** — the hard receipt gate now passes\n\n`wave5-spine-audit.json` now exists, so the blocker I handed back twice is cleared. Ledger at 114 rows. Record appended to `research/audit/wave5-alpha.md`; the append is reproducible via `research/audit/wave5-a8r3-write-adjudications.mjs`, which computes hashes rather than transcribing them.\n\nFor A10, the headline is that five of six are the same **fact-fidelity policy question** on its fifth unanswered wave (~75 of the wave's 91 nonfatals) — the library has no rule on whether a fact may carry a clause one step from its citation. Until one is written, both lanes keep finding it and every wave spends a round on it."
